What bug is present in this loop?

for (int i = 10; i >= 0; i++) {
    System.out.println(i);
}

What will this code print?

int x = 1;
while (x <= 3) {
    System.out.print(x + " ");
    // x++; is missing!
    break;
}

practice.problemStatement:
The following program intended to count down from 3 to 1, but it freezes due to an accidental semicolon bug and wrong step direction:

int x = 3;
while (x > 0);
    x++;

Fix the code in the Main class so it prints:
Countdown: 3
Countdown: 2
Countdown: 1
Liftoff!

practice.initialCode:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // BUGGY CODE TO FIX:
        int x = 3;
        // Fix the loop below:

    }
}

practice.solutionCode:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int x = 3;
        while (x > 0) {
            System.out.println("Countdown: " + x);
            x--;
        }
        System.out.println("Liftoff!");
    }
}

